# rena0-round-timeout — F1-3 fixture
# Expectations cite the economy's timed-round path: a round with `timeLimit` set is timed
# (`match_economy.h:318-320`), and the round ends through `RoundEnd::Timeout` — measured
# here as enum value 2 — with the losing side's balloon at 0 (MatchFrame::roundOver,
# MatchEconomy::roundEnd/balloon; FUN_00635d40 per the port's own comment).
combo 0 0
seed 5489
spawn 0 0 0 0
spawn 1 0 0 2000
time_limit 2
collision open-field
expect 59 round_over 0
expect 60 round_over 1
expect 60 round_end 2
expect 60 balloon1 0
#
# Finding recorded while authoring: the round clock also runs during the 60-update
# BattleStart, so `time_limit 1` (a 60-update clock) expires before this fixture's tick 0
# and the round is already over there. A 2-second limit leaves exactly 60 updates after
# startup, which is why the transition sits between updates 59 and 60.
